/* tests/negative/ — this file MUST FAIL to compile, with a clear error.
 *
 * `_Pragma` inside a macro body: §6.10.9 defines the pragma at the *invocation*
 * site, relative to the tokens around the call. A source-level expander has no
 * position to place it, so jetic refuses instead of dropping the pragma
 * somewhere harmless-looking.
 *
 * Expected (exit != 0), from the preprocessor's macro-expansion step:
 *
 *     Macro expansion failed:
 *     [cpp] line 18: macro 'PUSH' has '_Pragma' in its body, which jeti cannot
 *     expand — '_Pragma' (ISO/IEC 9899:2011 §6.10.9) takes effect at the
 *     invocation site during preprocessing, and a source-level expander has no
 *     position to place it; write the _Pragma(...) directly on its own source
 *     line instead
 *
 * Fix: write the `_Pragma(...)` on its own source line (see
 * tests/golden/36_macros/pragma_passthrough.jeti), or drop the pragma.
 */
#define PUSH _Pragma("clang diagnostic push")
#define POP  _Pragma("clang diagnostic pop")

int main(void) {
    PUSH
    return 0;
    POP
}
